      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I strongly advise against taking excessive melatonin or ibuprofen, especially without consulting a doctor, as they can have serious side effects, interact with other medications, or worsen the underlying issue. Melatonin is typically recommended for short-term use (up to 3 days) and for specific conditions, such as jet lag or insomnia, whereas ibuprofen is best used for short-term, mild pain relief. Drinking a small amount of juice or warm tea, such as ginger or chamomile, may also help ease your headache and dizziness, but be cautious not to overdo it.",
